WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.268
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with my family

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.069
and it does seem like Dad's

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.936
maybe wrapping up. Mom, you want

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:04.771
to unmute him real quick?

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.073
-So --
-Alright.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.109
-[ Laughs ]
-So, anyway, it's a great story.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.244
It's one of Hilary's favorites,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.378
[ Laughter ]
so, I'm glad I was able

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:13.680
to tell it tonight.
-It was really good.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.415
It was really good, Dad.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.016
-Everybody here liked it a lot.
-You know what?

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:20.286
I can't hear the audience,
really, being remote like this,

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.322
but I really just got the sense
that they really enjoyed it.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:24.457
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.591
They really, really loved it.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.794
-Just from the expressions
on your faces,

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.595
I think it really tracked
with them.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.231
[ Laughter ]
Thank you so much.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.364
I'm glad you guys liked it.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:34.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.869
-No, yeah, give him his round
of applause. Well-deserved.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.873
So, you guys showed up,
came over.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.309
First thing you did was stop
at the apartment, my apartment.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.877
I was here at work.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.046
-You got in early, couldn't
check into your hotel yet.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.715
Did you enjoy? Were you happy
to come to my apartment?

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.383
Was it, uh, hospital --
hospitable?

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.818
-It's colder
inside than outside.

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:53.686
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.522
-Like in New York, in November.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.825
And your television
doesn't work.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.027
-Nope.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.729
[ Laughter ]
-There's mustard, I think,

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.297
in the fridge,
but not much else.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.599
-No, we always like
to have one jar of mustard.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.034
It's a way of letting
our guests know they're welcome.

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.203
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:14.073
So, yeah.
-Now, what are your requests

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.441
when you come stay at a home?

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:16.909
We've left a spoiler.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.645
There's been an Easter egg
already in this interview.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.246
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.413
-Alright.

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:24.316
Beverages.
See, I drink sparkling water.

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:26.386
I drink grapefruit juice.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.688
I drink gin, I drink tonic,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.089
and sometimes I'll drink beer

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.091
and sometimes I'll drink wine.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.058
-Now, what do we have?

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:34.360
-Water.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.228
[ Laughter ]
-Not even sparkling water.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.463
-No, it comes right
from the tap.

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.431
-I know.
-[ Smooch ]

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.333
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.201
Look, you're getting
your free drinks elsewhere.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.469
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.271
-Well, you did make
a special trip

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.906
and went out and bought gin
and soda.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.540
-I made a mistake, yeah.
-Everyone loves

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.709
a nice gin and soda.
-I knew my mom was coming and I

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.810
went out to get gin and tonic

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.177
and I accidentally
got gin and soda,

00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:53.780
a drink no one orders.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.714
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:59.018
Now, Josh, one of the other
things that has been --

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.586
I guess you've had to be
a little creative,

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:01.954
in recent years,
about Thanksgiving

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.890
and, in general, you're a vegan,
now, for how many years?

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.159
-Coming on three.
-Coming on three.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.461
And recently visited
Mom and Dad.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.462
And you, very sweetly,
went out of your way

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:12.365
to make sure
that he was taken care of.
-Yeah.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.334
Kale and chickpea
and it was a soup with --

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.602
-So, what kind of soup was it?

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.938
Like a kale-chickpea soup?
-Kale-chickpea soup, yep.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.073
-Was it good, Josh?
-Yeah, it was a New York Times

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.208
recipe, I want to say.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.442
-Like she cut it out special

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.979
-Delicious.
-and prepped for my arrival.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:29.148
-You, as a son,
you must feel loved

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.583
when that happened.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.418
-Dad, was there any errors
in the soup?

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.955
[ Alert chimes ]
-Just one.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.623
[ Laughter ]
I mean, there were a lot

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:40.293
of ingredients and a lot to do.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.896
The problem was that, instead
of using vegetable broth --

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.265
she came so close and --

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.066
[ Laughter ]
very close.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.735
But she used chicken broth.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.803
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.
-So, it wasn't vegan.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.171
-Yeah.
And, now, did you --

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.107
-That's probably
why it was so good, but...

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.841
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.841 --> 00:03:00.579
...it wasn't vegan and Josh came
down the next morning and said,

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:03.116
"Did you use chicken broth
in that soup?

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.351
Because my stomach's
a little upset."

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.919
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:09.255
But she came really close.
-She really came close.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.823
You know, if there's only one
ingredient in there,

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.591
that's pretty close.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:13.659
I tried.
-You know, the thing is --

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.194
Yeah.
-You know, one would say

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.197
you could maybe be
as forgiving about gin and soda.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.431
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:21.167
One could say that.
-One could say that.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.135
-One could say that.
-The thing that concerns me is

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.137
that I know she's been trying
to poison me,

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:27.173
but I never thought she'd try
to poison Josh.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.907
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that's true.

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:30.309
That's about --

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:31.978
Once you get a taste
of the poisoning,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.947
you just start doing it
to everyone.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:36.482
But, Josh, anyway, it is --

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.318
I do hope -- I know
you're going back to L.A.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.153
I do hope you have
a great vegan Thanksgiving.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:42.888
-Yeah, I will.
And I don't like --

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.991
I know it gets tedious
for like vegans

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.925
to talk about being vegans...
-Yeah.

00:03:46.925 --> 00:03:48.293
-...but I did write a song
about it

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:49.795
[ Laughter ]
and I don't know
if I can sing that.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.898
-Oh, we don't have time, but --
-No, perfect, perfect.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.198
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:56.302 line:0%
[ Band play bright tune ]

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.552 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:22.528 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:30.970 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.511 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:00.933 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:01.934
Hey, Seth, do you think

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.068
animals like you?

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:04.403
-I don't think about it at all.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:05.604
[ Laughter ]
-Well, they probably don't,

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:06.806
because you eat them,

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.374
but I wrote a verse
about how they like me.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.175
Can I sing that one?
-We are out of time.

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:11.811
-2, 3, 4.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.419 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
Ooh!

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.587 line:0%
Big and plump.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.388 line:0%
I like that.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.289 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.831 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:48.414 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Sighs ]

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.781
Look at this.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.350
[ Crunch ]
Mmm!

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.318
Oh!

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.920
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.389
Ooh! Ooh!

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.223
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.125
Man.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.225
This is raw.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:02.861
[ Laughter ]
Unsalted.

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:03.528
[ Crunch ]

00:06:03.528 --> 00:06:05.598
Mmm!
Mmm.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.498
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.033
-Is that the same nut?

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.536
[ Laughter ]
-Mmm.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.005
Mmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.907
Wow!

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.108
Oh!
It was a big nut.

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:18.077
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.078 line:0%
Eli.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.837 line:0%
♪ And, oh, if tofu
is too gross for you ♪

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.641 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.582 --> 00:06:58.918 line:0%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:02.888
-Josh Meyers with the new
Thanksgiving vegan anthem.

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:05.191
We'll be right back
